('The Self-Help Trap (nyhetsbrev)','Tim Ferriss','Let’s pretend that life is the game of soccer. You can work on the mechanics of soccer by yourself. You can always get better at dribbling, shooting, and running drills as a solo practitioner. You can read dozens of books, study tape, and earn a PhD in the physics of ball flight. You can post videos of stunning shots on YouTube and get showered by emojis. But none of this is actually playing the game of soccer. You can spend your whole life preparing for, instead of playing, the game of life.','9'),
